## Current deployment status

- AKS `azaksrwgomixitryy6` is Ready with two `Standard_D2as_v7` nodes. The two-node size was approved after the subscription's four-vCPU quota prevented the original three-node plan.
- Redis is Ready (1/1) and workers are Ready (3/3).
- Updated the Event Hubs OAuth audience to the namespace-specific scope required by the Event Hubs Kafka sample; the focused test suite passes (8 tests). The patched `1.0.1` images are pushed and applied.
- AKS assigned public IP `48.194.77.114` to the API LoadBalancer Service with the user's approval for a temporary HTTP demo link. `/health/live`, `/health/ready`, and `/docs` returned HTTP 200 from outside the cluster.
- Latest deployment status: 2 of 3 API replicas Ready; Redis (1/1) and workers (3/3) Ready. Older API logs showed broker transport timeouts; end-to-end event processing has not been confirmed. This is demo access, not a production availability claim.
- Event Hubs public network access is enabled, DNS resolves in the API pod, and the deployment host can reach TCP 9093. AKS-to-Event-Hubs reachability still needs diagnosis.
- The API Service is temporarily `LoadBalancer` at `http://48.194.77.114` for presentation. HTTP exposes bearer tokens in transit; use demo-only credentials and revert to `ClusterIP` after the presentation. Do not report end-to-end event processing as verified.
